1b:["$","p","The issue is not only screen size. It is context. A visitor may start reading on the outer display, open the device for more detail, and continue into a contact form in the wider view. If the layout depends on a few rigid points, that transition exposes weak spots quickly.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"The issue is not only screen size. It is context. A visitor may start reading on the outer display, open the device for more detail, and continue into a contact form in the wider view. If the layout depends on a few rigid points, that transition exposes weak spots quickly."}]
1c:["$","section","Breakpoints are not a strategy",{"id":"section-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-heading font-semibold text-ink","children":"Breakpoints are not a strategy"}],[["$","p","A classic setup often looks like this: one layout up to 768 px, another from 1024 px, and a third for desktop. That can work for basic pages, but foldable web design demands thinking between those values. What happens at 820 px? At 912 px? What if the screen is wide, but not very tall?",{"className":"text-muted","children":"A classic setup often looks like this: one layout up to 768 px, another from 1024 px, and a third for desktop. That can work for basic pages, but foldable web design demands thinking between those values. What happens at 820 px? At 912 px? What if the screen is wide, but not very tall?"}],["$","p","Responsive web design should not depend on guessing every possible device. A better approach is to let content change layout when it runs out of room. In other words: the breakpoint should follow the content, not a phone model catalogue.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"Responsive web design should not depend on guessing every possible device. A better approach is to let content change layout when it runs out of room. In other words: the breakpoint should follow the content, not a phone model catalogue."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","The headline must remain readable without breaking into one word per line.",{"children":"The headline must remain readable without breaking into one word per line."}],["$","li","Navigation must not cover the primary call to action.",{"children":"Navigation must not cover the primary call to action."}],["$","li","Cards, images, and forms need fluid widths, not fixed assumptions.",{"children":"Cards, images, and forms need fluid widths, not fixed assumptions."}],["$","li","The contact journey should work on both the outer and inner display.",{"children":"The contact journey should work on both the outer and inner display."}]]}],"$undefined"]}]
1d:["$","section","Fluid design beats chasing every device",{"id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-heading font-semibold text-ink","children":"Fluid design beats chasing every device"}],[["$","p","Fluid design means elements adapt to the space they actually have. That includes flexible grids, sensible maximum widths, stable image ratios, text that does not become too wide, and components that can move from two columns to one without sudden breakage.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"Fluid design means elements adapt to the space they actually have. That includes flexible grids, sensible maximum widths, stable image ratios, text that does not become too wide, and components that can move from two columns to one without sudden breakage."}],["$","p","For a mobile website, that matters a lot. A site can look fine on one iPhone model and still fall apart on a device with a different aspect ratio or an open inner display. If the design depends on a fixed width, devices like iPhone Duo simply make the issue visible sooner.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"For a mobile website, that matters a lot. A site can look fine on one iPhone model and still fall apart on a device with a different aspect ratio or an open inner display. If the design depends on a fixed width, devices like iPhone Duo simply make the issue visible sooner."}]],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
1e:["$","section","Testing has to follow real user behaviour",{"id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-heading font-semibold text-ink","children":"Testing has to follow real user behaviour"}],[["$","p","Opening the homepage on one phone and declaring the site responsive is no longer enough. Testing should follow a task: find a service, open the menu, read a trust signal, and send an enquiry. If that journey breaks in one place, visitors will not think about breakpoints; they will just leave.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"Opening the homepage on one phone and declaring the site responsive is no longer enough. Testing should follow a task: find a service, open the menu, read a trust signal, and send an enquiry. If that journey breaks in one place, visitors will not think about breakpoints; they will just leave."}],["$","p","The useful minimum is a narrow mobile view, a larger phone, tablet widths, laptop, and large desktop. For foldable devices, pay special attention to medium widths and orientation changes. Chrome DevTools and similar tools help, but real devices and manual testing still reveal details simulation can miss.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"The useful minimum is a narrow mobile view, a larger phone, tablet widths, laptop, and large desktop. For foldable devices, pay special attention to medium widths and orientation changes. Chrome DevTools and similar tools help, but real devices and manual testing still reveal details simulation can miss."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Check whether horizontal scrolling appears.",{"children":"Check whether horizontal scrolling appears."}],["$","li","Move through the menu and contact form with a keyboard.",{"children":"Move through the menu and contact form with a keyboard."}],["$","li","Watch whether images load without shifting content.",{"children":"Watch whether images load without shifting content."}],["$","li","Test the main CTA button across several viewport widths.",{"children":"Test the main CTA button across several viewport widths."}]]}],"$undefined"]}]
1f:["$","section","Why 'it works on a phone' is no longer enough",{"id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-heading font-semibold text-ink","children":"Why 'it works on a phone' is no longer enough"}],[["$","p","The phrase 'it works on a phone' often means only that the page opens and the text is not completely broken. That is not enough for a website that should generate enquiries. The mobile version of a site needs to guide the visitor, explain the offer, load quickly, and show the next step clearly.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"The phrase 'it works on a phone' often means only that the page opens and the text is not completely broken. That is not enough for a website that should generate enquiries. The mobile version of a site needs to guide the visitor, explain the offer, load quickly, and show the next step clearly."}],["$","p","iPhone Duo is a useful prompt to check that now, before new formats become ordinary. A truly responsive site does not depend on one ideal screen. It behaves consistently across a range of devices, from a narrow phone to a larger inner display.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"iPhone Duo is a useful prompt to check that now, before new formats become ordinary. A truly responsive site does not depend on one ideal screen. It behaves consistently across a range of devices, from a narrow phone to a larger inner display."}]],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
20:["$","section","How does your website look on the new generation of devices?",{"id":"section-7","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-heading font-semibold text-ink","children":"How does your website look on the new generation of devices?"}],[["$","p","If you are not sure, that is exactly where a quick review helps. NMark Designs can check how your website behaves across key viewport widths, where the message gets weaker, and whether the contact journey stays clear.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"If you are not sure, that is exactly where a quick review helps. NMark Designs can check how your website behaves across key viewport widths, where the message gets weaker, and whether the contact journey stays clear."}],["$","p","Send the URL and request a free NMark audit. You will get concrete notes, not an abstract opinion: what is visible, where the issue appears, and which next step makes the most sense for your site.",{"className":"text-muted","children":"Send the URL and request a free NMark audit. You will get concrete notes, not an abstract opinion: what is visible, where the issue appears, and which next step makes the most sense for your site."}]],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
